  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Bhima vs State (2024:Rj-Jd:21154) on 8 May, 2024 Author: Farjand Ali Bench: Farjand Ali [2024:Rj-Jd:21154] High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan At Jodhpur S.B. Criminal Revision Petition No. 26/2003 Bhima S/o Shri Pema Gurjar, R/o Village Puthol, P.S. Rajnagar, District Rajsamand ----Petitioner Versus State of Rajasthan ----Respondent For Petitioner(s) : Mr. Naresh Singh For Respondent(s) : Mr. Mahipal Bishnoi, Pp Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Farjand Ali Order 08/05/2024 1.",
    "facts": "Bereft of elaborate details, facts relevant and essential for disposal of the instant criminal revision are that on 18.06.1986, the Food Inspector, Udaipur found the present petitioner selling [2024:RJ-JD:21154] (2 of 5) [CRLR-26/2003] goat milk without having licence for the same. The Food Inspector collected the sample of the milk following the prescribed procedure and sent the same for analysis to Public Analyst, Udaipur, from where a report was received mentioning that the sample of milk contained about 78% water, upon which, after obtaining prosecution sanction, a complaint was submitted against the petitioner in the competent court. The Learned Magistrate framed charge against the petitioner for the offence under Section 7/16 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act and upon denial of guilt by him, commenced the trial. During the course of trial, the prosecution in order to prove the offence, examined as many as 2 witnesses and exhibited various documents. The accused, upon being confronted with the prosecution allegations, in his statement under Section 313 CrPC, denied the allegations and claimed to be innocent. No evidence was adduced from the defence side. Aggrieved by the judgment of conviction, he preferred an appeal, which too has been dismissed by the learned appellate court. Hence, this revision petition is filed before this court.",
    "arguments": "4. After arguing the case on merits to some extent, learned counsel appearing for the petitioner submits that he will not assail conviction of the petitioner and confines his arguments to the alternative prayer of reduction of the sentence awarded by the [2024:RJ-JD:21154] (3 of 5) [CRLR-26/2003] trial court. He submits that the incident in the present case pertains to the year 1986. The petitioner has already suffered agony of protracted trial of 37 years. He has remained in custody for some time after passing of the judgment in appeal. He was not having any criminal antecedents and it was the first criminal case registered against him. No adverse remark has been passed over his conduct except the impugned judgment. No fruitful purpose would be served by sending him back to jail after lapse of such a long period. With these submissions, learned counsel prays that by taking a lenient view, the sentence awarded to the petitioner may be reduced to the period already undergone.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. After arguing the case on merits to some extent, learned counsel appearing for the petitioner submits that he will not assail conviction of the petitioner and confines his arguments to the alternative prayer of reduction of the sentence awarded by the [2024:RJ-JD:21154] (3 of 5) [CRLR-26/2003] trial court. He submits that the incident in the present case pertains to the year 1986. The petitioner has already suffered agony of protracted trial of 37 years. He has remained in custody for some time after passing of the judgment in appeal. He was not having any criminal antecedents and it was the first criminal case registered against him. No adverse remark has been passed over his conduct except the impugned judgment. No fruitful purpose would be served by sending him back to jail after lapse of such a long period. With these submissions, learned counsel prays that by taking a lenient view, the sentence awarded to the petitioner may be reduced to the period already undergone.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
